# Rendering an ordinary block as html used to abort the process with a
# Rust panic in the markup emitter's state machine (eu-1tkk.7.24).
#
# The block is nested deliberately. A single flat block never reached the
# panic — it fell out of the state machine as empty output and exit 0. The
# panic needed a block inside a block, which is exactly what
# `eu -x html file.eu` with no target produces: the unit's own block
# wrapping each of its declarations.
` { target: :main format: :html }
main: {
  page: { a: 1 b: 2 }
}
